"hint": "Step off the upper refuge to bait the first leftward charge, then jump, dash upward and steer right back to safety. Folding now drops the brute into the sealed left bay. Instead, return to the exposed right end of the dock to draw a rightward charge, then escape back to the refuge. The fixed buffer stops the brute above the useful bay. Walk off the refuge’s right edge, land on the upper bank, then drop through it and walk left under the screen to the operating shelf, make a small hop and strike left at the hub to fold the dock. Dash down-left into the descent line. From the receiving perch, drop to bait the lower wall, then jump and dash back up. The finish uses two ordinary hops.",
